  "task": {
    "objective": "Sustain six settlements' grain and transport while managing a shared sequential river: coordinate tools, physical handoffs, dams, bridges and barges; weigh local storage and flood protection against downstream water and navigation.",
    "natural_termination": "No natural success or joint-failure terminal. This is a continuing finite world. H=512 truncates the observation window, not a success event; done inputs are absorbing.",
    "interaction": "Opening an upstream sluice releases visible units into a three-position delayed river queue. Levees protect their own field and can increase downstream releases. A gate, low water or sediment can stop another settlement's loaded barge. Grain/timber handoffs and tool swaps are physical inventory transfers; direct home knowledge differs, and nearby speech sends expiring snapshots.",
    "observation_access": "All terrain, territories, actor inventories/tools, fields, woodlots, river levels/gates/levees/bridges/sediment, water packets, barges, rain, public event channels and reward components are public. A granary's current contents and rain phase code are directly visible only to its four home members via village_visible. Observations include only the observing actor's notes_food, notes_weather and note_life rows; a nearby speaker can provide a stale snapshot about their own settlement. Public actions and realized rain may permit inference; the source does not claim permanent secrecy against history. Legal foreign deposit attempts do not expose a full-granary test."
  },
