  "reward_components": [
    "Settlement stock and meals: +0.8 to each member of the destination settlement per deposited grain, -0.8 per own-granary withdrawal, plus +0.7 per actually consumed local meal",
    "Carrier stock potential: +0.2 to the depositing actor and -0.2 to the withdrawing actor per grain",
    "Public infrastructure/navigation: +0.15 to every actor per first-ever bridge and +0.02 per currently navigable reach on a hydraulic phase",
    "Costs: -0.02 per movement/interaction effort, -0.08 per timber spent, and -0.05 per grain sown",
    "Local harm: -0.4 per home field flood and -0.6 per home meal time with an empty granary"
  ],
  "reward_bound_derivation": "Deposits and withdrawals use signed changes so taking grain out and returning it does not create new aggregate stock credit. Trade moves this potential between settlements; meal reward requires grain consumption. A loose per-actor upper bound is 24*0.8 destination potential +0.7 meal +0.2 courier +6*0.15 first bridges +5*0.02 navigability =21.1, below declared 24. Only the four home actors can withdraw from a given granary, so a member can lose at most 4*0.8 plus personal 0.2, effort/material 0.18 and local flood/hunger 1.0, greater than -6. Native observed counts are at most 512 for t and at most 32 for stocks; signed knowledge sentinels and component rewards fit [-6,512]. These are analytic enclosing bounds, not measured returns.",
